    "updated_at": "2021-07-27T05:22:32Z",
    "body": "I run that to make sure that I'm running zsh installed by nix, not pre-installed one.\r\n\r\nI also tried installing starship as one of packages in `home.packages`, rather than as a module. and run `eval \"$(starship init zsh)\" directly. It didn't make any difference.\r\n\r\nI didn't use starship module's settings option. So it just adds starship packages, and adds following to zsh shell configuration. I guess that's why installing directly doesn't make any difference.\r\nhttps://github.com/nix-community/home-manager/blob/f6f6990fc811454cb3082ba3662b711488fd0554/modules/programs/starship.nix#L97-L101\r\n\r\nI've found that starship works correctly on bash, so this seems to be something specific to zsh.",
